## Wave 10J Lessons (2026-04-24)

### Pattern: GATE-CL gates are aspirational without enforcement scripts
GATE-CL1-5 were added to the SOP checklist in Wave 10I.C but were never applied to any pair — no verification script exists. A gate that exists only in text is an aspiration, not a gate. Every gate requires either a script or a documented <5-minute manual checklist that is actually run.

### Pattern: NBER shading is 100% Vera's domain — no app-side injection
load_plotly_chart() is a pure deserialiser (pio.from_json → st.plotly_chart). No add_vrect, no NBER date logic, no shading injection exists anywhere in charts.py or page_templates.py. When NBER shading is missing from a chart, the fix is always in Vera's JSON, never in the template.

### Pattern: Cross-period template wiring pattern
render_evidence_page() now has a Cross-Period Consistency section. Always renders subperiod_sharpe, rolling_correlation, structural_break. Conditionally renders rolling_sharpe, rolling_granger when method_blocks.get("EVIDENCE_CONFIG", {}).get("regime_story") is True. Missing files → st.info("Cross-period analysis pending"), never st.error.

## ACE-HZE1 — History Zoom Episodes: the silent-omission class (2026-04-24)

- **The three-agent chain with no closing link.** Ray delivers `history_zoom_episodes` in narrative frontmatter. Vera generates `history_zoom_{slug}.json` chart files. The template renders the "How the Signal Performed in Past Crises" section when `HISTORY_ZOOM_EPISODES` is defined on the config. But Ace had no rule requiring it to close the loop — no step in the pair-config authorship workflow said "read Ray's handoff and populate this field." Result: 8 of 9 pair configs omit the field, the section silently disappears, and no error surfaces anywhere in smoke, cloud verify, or QA.
- **Silent skip is always a process gap in disguise.** When a template section silently disappears because a config field is absent, it feels like a deliberate optional feature. It is actually a missing SOP rule. The correct test: "Would a QA observer looking at the rendered page know the section was supposed to be there?" If the answer is no, the absence is indistinguishable from a deliberate omission — invisible to all quality gates. The fix is always a rule, not a fallback.
- **ACE-HZE1 closes the gap.** New rule: at config-authorship time, Ace audits Ray's handoff and Vera's chart directory. If either has episode data, the field MUST be populated. If the other side hasn't delivered, Ace files a blocker — does not silently omit. Chart absent → Vera blocker. Narrative absent → Ray blocker (hard block, LEAD-DL1 forbids Ace authoring narrative).
- **Cross-agent chains require explicit handoff reads at every link.** The pattern generalises: any time Ace builds a config that feeds a template feature, Ace must read all upstream handoffs (Ray, Vera, Evan) for every field the template can render. Passive "I'll populate it when I see it" is not sufficient — the authorship checklist must enumerate every config field and the upstream source to read for it.

## 2026-04-24 — Wave 10J/10K Self-Reflection

### What went well
- Structural delivery volume with LEAD-DL1 discipline: 15 legacy pages migrated, 7 pair configs authored, zero role-boundary violations on producer artifacts.
- Root-cause tracing in Wave 10I.A Fix: identified cloud traceback as red herring, traced real short-circuit to `position_adjustment_panel.py:177`, documented 3 remediation options with scope assignments.
- APP-RL1 single-source routing delivered proactively — identified dual-definition hazard and fixed architecturally without being dispatched.

### What fell short
- GATE-CL1-5 are aspirational, not operational. No `scripts/gate_cl_audit.py` exists. Gates written as SOP prose without enforcement tooling are not gates — they are intentions. This is a planning failure: the enforcement step was never budgeted into the gate-definition wave scope.
- Pattern failure: GATE-27 (APP-ST1 loader smoke) also preceded its tooling. The pattern of defining gates before their scripts must stop.

### Role-boundary root cause
When Ace authors a gate, it is natural to document the full lifecycle including verification steps. But "QA must confirm X" belongs in the QA SOP, not Ace's. Two failure modes: Quincy may not see it (doesn't read Ace's SOP at SOD), and Ace gains cover to skip it ("that's Quincy's gate"). Fix: at next SOP revision, audit every gate description and remove any verification steps naming a downstream agent as actor.

### Open issues
- `scripts/gate_cl_audit.py` — Wave 10K Phase 1, non-negotiable.
- HY-IG v2 reference pair still on hand-written pages — new agents learn old pattern first.
- `signal`/`signal_code`/`signal_column` or-chain fallback in page_templates.py — META-CF debt.

### Key lessons to carry forward
1. Gate text and enforcement script must ship in the same commit, or the gate is ASPIRATIONAL with a backlog item and wave target.
2. Silent structural changes to legacy bypass pages need explicit callouts in handoff even when additive.

## 2026-04-24 — META-CPD: commit without push is not a completed deliverable

In Wave 10J and Wave 10K, agents (including Ace) committed SOP and portal changes but did not immediately push to origin main. This caused wasted Streamlit Cloud reboots because the cloud deploy did not reflect the committed state — reviewers and Quincy's cloud-verify were operating on a stale deployment. A commit that is not pushed is invisible to the cloud and to any team member who pulls. META-CPD (documented in team-coordination.md) formalizes the rule: every `git commit` must be immediately followed by `git push origin main`. This applies to all agents including Ace, and explicitly to SOP commits.

**How to apply:** After every `git commit`, run `git push origin main` as the very next command. Do not batch pushes. Do not defer pushes to "end of wave." A commit without a push is not a completed deliverable.

## 2026-06-17 -- New-pair APP-PT1 rendered probe pattern

- **Smoke-loader PASS is necessary but not sufficient for new template pairs.** In `petrol_inv_spy`, loader smoke passed all 20 charts, but a focused local DOM probe caught two user-visible consumer drifts: `lead_value` was ignored so Strategy showed `LN/A`, and the probability panel still said `long XLV` on an SPY page.
- **Current winner summaries may use `lead_value`.** When rendering lead labels, read `lead_months -> lead_value -> lead_days`, then display the normalized label everywhere. A single corrected title is not enough; scan for every `L{_lead}` display site.
- **Probe each Streamlit tab as active.** `inner_text("body")` only exposes the active tab. For Strategy pages, click Execute, Performance, and Confidence separately and assert required markers plus absence of APP-SEV1/stub strings.

Evidence: `python app/_smoke_tests/smoke_loader.py petrol_inv_spy` -> 20/0; `python app/_smoke_tests/smoke_schema_consumers.py --pair-id petrol_inv_spy` -> 5/0; focused local Playwright probe -> landing, four pages, and Strategy tabs PASS.

