### Wave 10G.4E-fix (2026-04-22) — two cloud bugs fixed
- Bug 1: `pair_registry.py` `page_routing` dict was missing `hy_ig_spy` → added `"hy_ig_spy": "pages/15_hy_ig_spy"`. Rule: add routing entry in same commit as page wrappers.
- Bug 2: `probability_engine_panel._validate_signal` unpacked stress windows as 2-tuples, but `interpretation_metadata.json` uses dicts `{label, start, end, note}`. Added `_to_window()` normaliser; both tuple and dict forms now accepted.
- Smoke tests do NOT exercise `st.page_link` — page routing bugs are cloud-only. Always add routing entry at pair-build time.
- Commit: 75d6574

### Wave 10G.5-fix (2026-04-22) — APP-RL1: deleted _page_prefix, unified routing

- Bug A: `_page_prefix()` in `page_templates.py` had its own copy of `page_routing` dict. Wave 10G.4E-fix added `hy_ig_spy` to `pair_registry.py`'s copy but forgot `page_templates.py` → `StreamlitPageNotFoundError` on cloud for hy_ig_spy Story + Evidence.
- Bug B: `indicator_names` in `load_pair_registry()` was missing `hy_ig_spy` → landing card showed `hy_ig_spread_pct`.
- Fix: module-level `PAGE_ROUTING = {...}` + `get_page_prefix(pair_id)` in `pair_registry.py`; deleted `_page_prefix()` from `page_templates.py`; replaced 3 call sites with `get_page_prefix` (imported at top). Added `"hy_ig_spy": "HY-IG Credit Spread"` to `indicator_names`.
- Commit: 35bb008
- Smoke: hy_ig_spy 6/0, hy_ig_v2_spy 15/0, indpro_xlp 8/0, umcsent_xlv 7/0.

## 2026-04-23 Wave 10H.1 follow-up

**Template-scope miss (recurrence guard):** Wired `_render_exploratory_insights` into `render_methodology_page()` in Wave 10H.1 e6767e0 but did not grep pages/ for bypass. Result: Sample pair (`9_hy_ig_v2_spy_methodology.py` — hand-written) silently skipped the section on cloud. Quincy hypothesized CWD/path bug; actual cause was template bypass. **Rule for self:** when modifying a centralized template, always run `grep -L "<template_function>" app/pages/*.py` to enumerate bypasses before closing. 5 hand-written methodology pages currently bypass the template in this codebase.

**Silent-fail vs surfaced-fail discipline:** APP-SEV1 L2 says path-exists-but-unreadable/JSON-parse failure on a shipped pair MUST surface. I originally wrapped `_render_exploratory_insights` read in `try/except (JSONDecodeError, OSError): return` which swallowed both the expected-silent case (missing file = legacy pair) and the real-bug case (malformed JSON). Now split: missing file = silent-skip, unreadable/malformed = `st.warning` with path + exception class. This makes cloud debugging tractable.

**Landing-card text leaks pipeline tokens:** `interpretation_metadata.json.key_finding` is a pipeline-generated sentence that contains raw column names (`spy_fwd_63d`). Any user-facing display of pipeline-generated text fields must pass through a humanize layer. Added `humanize_column_tokens()` + `_FWD_RETURN_LABELS` map in pair_registry.py as the SSoT.

